{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou","id":659504,"title":"Not knowing Which Children are Garou?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-10T10:26:12-07:00","id":659504,"title":"Not knowing Which Children are Garou?","content":"one major twist in anniversary edition is that NOTHING Can determine which child will go through the change... any ideas how massively this will change the way a kinfolk family works...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T10:47:37-07:00","id":659531,"title":"","content":"This was the way I'd always played, so...not at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T12:06:29-07:00","id":659674,"title":"","content":"It pretty much said that Scent of the true form could identify garou right after the change in 3rd edition... a lot of things like Marriages being planned in infancy, would be replaced with tenative feelers being sent out when their 6 or 7 amongst 3 or 4 familys, just to be ready, just in case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T12:07:25-07:00","id":659676,"title":"","content":"Where does it say that nothing can sense this? W20 change some low level stuff that used to be able to differentiate between kinfolk and pre-change potential Garou (a minor point in the books, but it is theoretically possible for a Garou to never undergo the change, but they're still Garou not kinfolk), to sensing them as the same thing.<br /> <br /> This is not the same thing as making it impossible to do. Baptism of Fire is kind of a pointless Rite if the Garou can't figure out the kinfolk kids from the true-born kids at all. Removing knowing this from a level 1 Gift just implies however its done is something either a bit rarer or higher ranking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T12:36:27-07:00","id":659723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=659676#post659676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baptism of Fire is kind of a pointless Rite if the Garou can't figure out the kinfolk kids from the true-born kids at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you just perform it on the Silver Fang Kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T12:48:16-07:00","id":659733,"title":"","content":"There's a talen called a Test Vial on page 384 that lets you tell garou from kin. That would work pre-change, wouldn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T13:01:01-07:00","id":659748,"title":"","content":"You know, not being able to tell Kin from full Changer until the change or shaping of Archid seems like it would be a potential cause a pretty high incidence of breaking the first tenet of the Litany and its equivalents among the Fera, especially if you get any late bloomers at all. Time goes past, everyone gives up on potential full changers, but surprise! They weren't actually &quot;just kin&quot; at all! Welcome to Charach Town, population you and the individual you thought was kin!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T14:24:35-07:00","id":659872,"title":"","content":"Hmmm that is a pickle. The Gift of Sense the True Form says that pre-Change garou smell like Kin. But the Rite Baptism of Fire says to perform it in the first month of the new borns birth...but that you'll need something like Sense the True Form to determine whether the child is Garou or not.<br /> <br /> First of choose whether you're doing it as Gaia chooses who will become Garou or not from birth. Then decide if you're going by w20 rules strictly as written.<br /> <br /> If yes, I'd say if the Rite of Baptism and Sense of the True Form are done at the same time within that first month then yes they can tell. If no one ever does it then no one will know until it happens.<br /> <br /> if you say no..I want garou detectable to Sense of the True Form from birth...then that's it. No surprises that way and all those rites and gifts work just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T14:37:08-07:00","id":659887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=659723#post659723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you just perform it on the Silver Fang Kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't make a lot of sense unless you're a very morally dubious Shadow Lord trying to undermine the Silver Fangs by making their kin even bigger targets for the BSDs.<br /> <br /> Baptism of Fire's main purpose is to alert the Tribe when a cub is in danger, and especial in danger of going through their first Change. But it has a done side of making it easier for any Garou (including BSDs) or spirits to know the child is marked. The Rite specifically calls out the BSDs look for kids with the spirit-brand the Rite creates to snatch kids away from the Gaian Garou. For a cub, the risk is worth it compared to the danger of no-warning first Changes. For a kin... all it does is make them a target.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=659733#post659733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a talen called a Test Vial on page 384 that lets you tell garou from kin. That would work pre-change, wouldn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason it wouldn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T15:36:52-07:00","id":659970,"title":"","content":"I For one prefer myself when thinking about it they not be able to know.... as them not being able to differentiate a PRe change Garou from a kinfolk, lets cases of children who grow up in the largest septs, and thus grow up KNOWING of their heritage, retain some degree of Dramatic tension in the backstory","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T15:47:17-07:00","id":659977,"title":"","content":"It makes it quite a bit more interesting if the Garou cannot be readily identified pre-change. It changes the impact and treatment of kinfolk quite a bit towards the better and it feeds into excellent stories about people and missed expectations. It's not that new an idea, it's supported by some of the in character fiction and I think that even there was something in Revised to that effect.<br /> <br /> I've also been running Werewolf like that since forever, so it's not a biggie for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T19:29:24-07:00","id":660229,"title":"","content":"I took the write up for Scent of True Form to mean a pre-Change Garou automatically detects as Kinfolk, but not that it is impossible to detect a pre-Change Garou as Garou. I'd allow one success on the roll will allow the Garou to detect it as an actual Garou. I'd also rule that two successes detects the Fera's Kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T15:04:06-07:00","id":663505,"title":"","content":"I think we can agree, that in 2nd and revised it was easy to learn whether a child was garou or not and that some children, like Anna Kliminski, were trained to be heir/heiress to their garou parent's legacy from early childhood on. That is: even pre-change.<br /> <br /> W20 changes that aspect of the game. Not only evident with &quot;Scent of the true Form&quot;, but also page 41, which states, that virtually any kinfolk could be garou (which is given as one reason why some tribes revere their kin). The same page also states that being garou is genetic.<br /> <br /> So, in my opinion, this part of W20 is crap. Period.<br /> <br /> The Test Vial (in W20) has no limitation about pre-change garou, but also doesn't state that they register as garou, either. It is up to the ST to rule on that - where revised had a clear ruling in the FAQ.<br /> In any case, the Vial is simply copy&amp;pasted from Kinfolk: Usung Heroes. And since we don't know if the person who was copying and pasting, is the same one who wrote page 41 or the limitation in &quot;Scent of the true form&quot;, this pretty much can be attributed to bad editing and/or not enough crowd editing aka open development. In any case, I assume garou would have wanted to know if their offspring was garou long before test vials came into existence, so the talen shouldn't be the only means of determining the answer to this question with relative certainty. Some herbs, rites, gifts, or other magical mumbo-jumbo should be out there. But, as I pointed out, W20, especially on page 41, clearly sets a mood towards &quot;garou don't know&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, the question was, &quot;How would the world/culture of the garou be, if they can not (and never could) know if their children are garou?&quot;<br /> And here is my take on that:<br /> <br /> The &quot;Baptism of Fire&quot; would not exist, or would be performed on any child. If it only works on garou, but doesn't impart the knowledge if it worked onto the performing ritemaster, the garou culture regarding kin families and offspring from one-night-stands could remain relatively the same, compared to a setting where the garou know. About when the first change is to happen, garou would get a kin-fetch spirit's alert and be there for the new garou and prevent any Veil lifting as good as they can.<br /> <br /> But, if that wasn't an option either, then the game world would be different, in my opinion. Having lost cubs without any means to find them would have lead to the Veil being lifted centuries ago. That is unless you rule in favour of divine intervention by Totems and such. But really, if some random people would become garou one day, sure some would hide the fact and be afraid of the government or big corporate, but at least one would hope he is save or gets famous if he demonstrated his powers on live TV.<br /> <br /> Only means to prevent that would be to forbid (and punish) all male garou, who impregnate a woman, who isn't aware of garou and who then removes the child from garou supervision. Although kidnapping such children and raising them, would probably solve the problem of them becoming lost cubs.<br /> <br /> Sex with kin obviously is the best option, as the Curse prevents garou from bringing humans into the fold (not withstanding a Rite which could). But wait, not all garou have their first change at puberty (also page 41). In earlier Editions such garou were crazy Lunatics, today it seems totally okay that they first change in their adulthood (which I find okay, from a character design standpoint). But, if only 1% of all garou doesn't change in puberty that means that one in 10.000 kin is secretly garou and will have a metis child, if having sex with a garou or another of the adult un-changed garou. With teenager sex, the chance of having sex with a garou and therefore become a metis-parent is 1 in 10. Great odds. So, the whole outlook on metis and metis-parents in the garou culture might change. I mean, metis by teenager pregnancy would be relatively common.<br /> <br /> As far as educating the offspring goes, kin and garou kids alike would get the full garou treatment, if the parent is in hope of a successor. This would lead to kin that is probably way more knowledgeable about garou and possibly more apart from normal humans. Also, possibly more kin secrets would be taught amongst the kin possibly raising the number of shaman-like sorcerers amongst their ranks.<br /> <br /> All in all, I have to say, that a garou culture, where garou can't discern if their children are garou, could be interesting, but it wouldn't be WtA!<br /> And it would have needed more changes than the write-up on page 41 and the changes to &quot;Scent of the true form&quot;. In my opinion, an author here wanted to impose his view of the game world onto us and didn't really put the effort in to make it coherent. And it stinks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 09-13-2015, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T15:34:20-07:00","id":663518,"title":"","content":"And for all that, I still believe the idea of Garou not knowing who will be Garou makes for better and more intriguing stories. Stories abour great expectations, parental dissapointment and bitterness of not being what you have hoped for all your youth. It's something I've introduced after my first session of Werewolf where one of my players actually came up with an amazing reasoning why he had a late first change, and how he had horrible relations with his family due to the way he was treated for not fulfilling their expectations.<br /> <br /> I also loved when a similar thing was introduced later with the coming of the Dragon Blooded, just with more machiavellian games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T03:19:03-07:00","id":664073,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure not being able to track who's going to change would be such a massive veil-breacher. Forsaken manages alright without it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T20:23:24-07:00","id":665293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=663505#post663505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Having lost cubs without any means to find them would have lead to the Veil being lifted centuries ago. That is unless you rule in favour of divine intervention by Totems and such. But really, if some random people would become garou one day, sure some would hide the fact and be afraid of the government or big corporate, but at least one would hope he is save or gets famous if he demonstrated his powers on live TV.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all Garou born had the Baptism of Fire performed for them especially in more modern nights. In earlier editions, there was an implied backstory that many Garou approaching their first change became runaways, driven by some inner need and wanderlust, and that other Garou somehow found them. Spirits and such may have played a role, but it doesn't require divine intervention by Incarna. It could be Ancestor Spirits guiding the newly aborning cub to somewhere he will be safe (this would be the easiest go-to scenario). There could be Galliard genealogists tracking extended family lines and asking spirits or kinfolk to keep their eyes and ears open, or that crazy &quot;great uncle&quot; who appears every now and again. There might be cryptic family secrets laid around that only make sense to people on the cusp of change, and which points them to the right direction.<br /> <br /> I agree that lost cubs create a greater risk something will go wrong, but I think there are ways around it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=663505#post663505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But wait, not all garou have their first change at puberty (also page 41). In earlier Editions such garou were crazy Lunatics, today it seems totally okay that they first change in their adulthood (which I find okay, from a character design standpoint).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily Lunatics. Lunatics are people who repress their wolf instincts to the point they can't transform, and the Beast drives them mad as a result. Not all late changing Garou fit that category. There could be various explanations on why they don't change during puberty, but which don't make them Lunatics. Instead, the Beast wakens only at a much later date. Perhaps they needed a specific trigger which they lacked during puberty. I think the likelihood of becoming a Lunatic increases the longer the Garou to be first changes, but it's also entirely possible that there are people should have transformed during puberty, but didn't because they were a Lunatic (they repressed the wolf even at such a young age). I think it's two different phenomenon, but there are some correlations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T09:22:18-07:00","id":665812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=664073#post664073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure not being able to track who's going to change would be such a massive veil-breacher. Forsaken manages alright without it.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does Forsaken do it? How do the werewolves there get the information, that another person is a werewolf?<br /> <br /> I remember vaguely, that they have a gift that allows them to track anyone they have bitten, which leads to them biting cubs, which in turn leads to the myth that bite causes being a werewolf. But I can't remember if they are told that there actually is a pre-change werewolf cub - or if they are supposed to find them by accident.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T09:28:08-07:00","id":665814,"title":"","content":"That's not actually a gift, it comes standard. <br /> <br /> Anyhow, generally speaking they know when a cub is right on the verge of turning because the spirit world goes mental around them. But they only get about a months warning. Before then it's impossible to tell the difference between a pre-change werewolf and a wolf blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T09:52:24-07:00","id":665824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=665293#post665293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all Garou born had the Baptism of Fire performed for them especially in more modern nights.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but it is written, that garou have a practice to steal children from distant relatives to perform the Rite before returning them. So my guess is, that the Rite is not performed on 100% of the cubs, but a majority. Also, the &quot;being kin to garou&quot;-trait isn't passed down amongst humans (or wolves) indefinitely. At some point the garou don't have to worry any more and just need to check on closer relatives and their offspring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=665293#post665293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In earlier editions, there was an implied backstory that many Garou approaching their first change became runaways, driven by some inner need and wanderlust, and that other Garou somehow found them. Spirits and such may have played a role, but it doesn't require divine intervention by Incarna. It could be Ancestor Spirits guiding the newly aborning cub to somewhere he will be safe (this would be the easiest go-to scenario).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that was if one would assume that ancestor spirits roamed the penumbra and had a domain-sense (my tribe) charm with a decent enough dice pool to find such cubs. But somehow I don't believe that this is the case.<br /> To paraphrase Stan Lee &quot;You can't just come up with origins for every character, having them bitten by radioactive spirders and such. At some point, they all are mutants and you go on with the story you want to tell.&quot;<br /> So, sure, every cub could be found by a variation of coincidence, luck, and convenience in their backstory. But, I don't find a whole cultures secrecy based on that unbelievable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=665293#post665293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There could be Galliard genealogists tracking extended family lines and asking spirits or kinfolk to keep their eyes and ears open, or that crazy &quot;great uncle&quot; who appears every now and again. There might be cryptic family secrets laid around that only make sense to people on the cusp of change, and which points them to the right direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, strangely enough there is not sept office or something that deals with such crap, although &quot;Silver Crown&quot; implies it is part of the seneschal's job in a Silver Fangs Court.<br /> Anyway, why have spirits asked to watch, or kin, if there is a perfectly good rite do to exactly that. I usually would ask for high rewards if a player tries to convince a spirit to do something that is traditionally done be a gift or rite. Simply because if the player hasn't put the effort into learning that gift/rite (or doesn't have the rank) than he probably isn't worthy of that particular service. I mean, there are traditions and such...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=665293#post665293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that lost cubs create a greater risk something will go wrong, but I think there are ways around it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, there are ways around it, and surely the garou could have come up with a lot of other ways, except the baptism of fire, but that is the one in the books. And it is bound on knowing if a child is garou or not - a fact that could have been changed in W20, maybe should have been changed, but wasn't.<br /> But that is besides the point, that garou would have come up with means to determine if a child is a garou or not. If they really hadn't, then they would have at least needed means to be warned about first changes that will happen soon. If there were other means, W20 fails to name them, and frankly, that would be an even greater change to the setting.<br /> In any case changing the setting like W20 does simply doesn't make sense. It's like garou being fighters, but somehow no healing gifts were available and the setting authors would hand-wave the topic just as if &quot;no garou ever thought to ask spirits for a magical healing gift&quot;.<br /> The need to know if a child is garou or not, or at least any other means to keep an eye on such a child, is kind of inherent to the way the world is described and it really is a no-brainer that such means are something garou would have aimed for. And such means were there until revised. No, suddenly authors tell us, such means didn't exist ever, were never invented in the millennia old garou culture - without filling the hole it creates in the logic of the game world ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=665293#post665293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not necessarily Lunatics. Lunatics are people who repress their wolf instincts to the point they can't transform, and the Beast drives them mad as a result. Not all late changing Garou fit that category. There could be various explanations on why they don't change during puberty, but which don't make them Lunatics. Instead, the Beast wakens only at a much later date. Perhaps they needed a specific trigger which they lacked during puberty. I think the likelihood of becoming a Lunatic increases the longer the Garou to be first changes, but it's also entirely possible that there are people should have transformed during puberty, but didn't because they were a Lunatic (they repressed the wolf even at such a young age). I think it's two different phenomenon, but there are some correlations.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I wrote &quot;earlier editions&quot; I meant 1st and 2nd edition werewolf, where becoming a Luntaic seemed inevitable, when one didn't have the first change in puberty. Revised toned down that bit a lot. That said, there wasn't any definitive rule on that part, at least I can't remember. So, even if haunted by strange dreams and their own instincts and going crazy, Lunatics could very well still have a first change if mentored correctly. But if such an experience would drive them even more crazy or not, was also open to interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 09-15-2015, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T20:03:20-07:00","id":666347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=665814#post665814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not actually a gift, it comes standard.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, generally speaking they know when a cub is right on the verge of turning because the spirit world goes mental around them. But they only get about a months warning. Before then it's impossible to tell the difference between a pre-change werewolf and a wolf blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay. That is a way to do it. If W20 had wanted such a mechanic too, they should have said so.<br /> <br /> I can't say that I would like such a situation very much, but I can accept that it works in Forsaken.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T18:30:40-07:00","id":679499,"title":"","content":"All pre-change Garou are kin folk through and through even if they are not aware of it. Any gifts that can tell the difference of a Garou from a Kin will show the target as kin until the first change occurs.<br /> <br /> Even the spirits are not 100% certain on the matter which is why the first change is always traumatic as there isn't kind uncle Garou waiting in the side lines to cart you off. Even if a kin is kept at near the caern as part of the sept the change is always a surprise and likly the rage that triggered the change would be the fault of other kin and Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/982-cptmachine","name":"Cptmachine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T19:06:59-07:00","id":679536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cptmachine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=679499#post679499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All pre-change Garou are kin folk through and through even if they are not aware of it. Any gifts that can tell the difference of a Garou from a Kin will show the target as kin until the first change occurs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Citation? Because to me, the rules are fairly clear that pre-change Garou are explicitly not Kin, even if some Gifts can't tell the difference. As well, there's no need to specify in Gifts that they can't tell the difference if there was a default rule that said they can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T14:09:07-07:00","id":681390,"title":"","content":"W20's page 41 is not 'hard' rules, but it implies that the discrimination between kin and pre-change Garou is not the rule within the game world. So no common gifts, rites, observation of recovery times from wounds and so on seem to do the trick. So, is two different things are not discernable as different, they aren't...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T15:55:22-07:00","id":681472,"title":"","content":"Saying that pre-Change Garou are Kinfolk because telling the difference is hard (though the books have changed a lot over four editions on this, without changing many setting assumption in the process) doesn't hold up. And the idea that just because you can't tell that two things are different, doesn't meant they are different has.... well... lots of holes in it as far as logic goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T18:38:14-07:00","id":682568,"title":"","content":"It is a basic thought experiment. I mean, where is the practical application? Sure, we as outside observers of the game world know that there are differences between kin and pre-change garou, but those are for the most part only relevant when the Firsting is near or happening. So, for the garou society there is a practical dilemma, for about 1 in ten of their offspring (as a people) is going to be something different than human (or wolf) but they can't be sure who precisely that is.<br /> So, foremost, they treat these offspring as one would treat kids, for that they are for sure. But besides that, once they aren't toddlers any more, the question arises if one would treat them all, as if they would become garou or as if they would not (if raised among the garou society that is).<br /> <br /> As I said before, I likes the Setting better, when garou could discern the difference and probably treated children differently. Although, I found that &quot;Scent of the true Form&quot; has a serious design flaw in allowing to detect garou with no roll. I would have it found best if pre-change garou could get a false negative result, and kin a false positive result with the gift, so that some character background possibilities arise, but the distinction should work in most cases. But, as I pointed out, W20 seems to work on another premise, setting another mood for the game. How that reflects on garou society in my opinion, I wrote earlier,,,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T01:27:50-07:00","id":682793,"title":"","content":"The uncertainty breeds stories, though. Imagine Kinfolk brought up to be great warriors and shamans... groomed and hoping to be the greatest heroes ever. And then disappointing their parents, disappointing themselves. How do they cope, how do they work with this society - do they become renegades or do they integrate and use their preparation to become key assets to the Garou nation? The other side of the coin is as enticing - the runt who noone appreciated becoming the chosen one, the insane son who everyone thought was harmless becoming Garou and the Lost Cubs who need guidance and do not understand the Garou Nation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T02:30:29-07:00","id":682847,"title":"","content":"Sure, but that all could also work in other ways. I mean, there were lost cubs, even when the garou could detect pre-change garou. My guess is, that they were rarer, but with the ability to find garou cubs and the baptism of fire there was no need to keep an too close eye on them. With W20 and no idea how one determines a child to be garou to apply the rite (as it still refers to Scent of the true form, although the gift lost this usage) the need to observe all relatives is increased hugely. And therefore the need to educate all children appropriately and therefore have a lot of kin, that is a lot more aware of garou culture is the result.<br /> <br /> But, before you had stories, where one sibling is garou and treated special, while the other(s) are not and probably start to resent their garou sibling. Now, all children are raised as equals, until the change comes - and, since W20 states it can come at any age after puberty, there is no need in being disappointed for it could still happen to you. And, as a matter of fact, you weren't told from the get go, that you aren't as good as you &quot;chosen&quot; sibling.<br /> <br /> Like I said, a level of uncertainty would have been fine and it should have come in the form of &quot;Scent of the true form&quot; being not absolute in discerning pre-change garou, but providing false positive and false negative results. The gift not working at all and leaving us hanging in regards to other means of detection, there is absolute uncertainty. And while it makes nice stories - it prohibits the possibility of &quot;One sibling was chosen, the other was not&quot;-scenarios. Along with possible changes to garou culture. So, the change didn't just give, it took away, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T06:58:01-07:00","id":683072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=682847#post682847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but that all could also work in other ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what's been confusing to me about the visceral reaction to W20. Both ways of being lead to interesting settings and stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T08:54:11-07:00","id":683216,"title":"","content":"I think part of the problem with W20 is that it doesn't seem to remember that this is a dial, and offer deliberate options in how to handle it. Instead, it lifts things from periods where the game assumes detecting pre-Change Garou is hard, and from periods when the game assumed it wasn't hard; then leaves them all in.<br /> <br /> Basically W20 took the worst of four options. It didn't outright take the side of, &quot;detect,&quot; it didn't outright take the side of, &quot;can't detect,&quot; it didn't treat this detection as a dial discussing the pros and cons of each approach, it left stuff for both sides in; often in fairly contradictory ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T21:11:13-07:00","id":683898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=682847#post682847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, a level of uncertainty would have been fine and it should have come in the form of &quot;Scent of the true form&quot; being not absolute in discerning pre-change garou, but providing false positive and false negative results. The gift not working at all and leaving us hanging in regards to other means of detection, there is absolute uncertainty. And while it makes nice stories - it prohibits the possibility of &quot;One sibling was chosen, the other was not&quot;-scenarios. Along with possible changes to garou culture. So, the change didn't just give, it took away, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is an easy way to accomplish this. With Scent of True form, the Garou automatically detects a pre-Change Garou as kin. However, if they roll, they have the chance of detecting the pre-Change Garou as really Garou. If the Garou botch the role, they get a false positive or false negative. It's probably best to have the PCs always roll - if they get no successes, then give them the automatic detection - don't give them the automatic success to begin with and then decide whether to roll.<br /> <br /> Botches, of course, will be rare, but I think it makes the uncertainty stories even stronger. After all, Garou will expect the initial test to be correct. In the example Asmodai gave, there is no real reason to groom offspring to become great Garou - 9 of 10 will fail. Why make the investment until the child changes? On the other hand, if the Scent of True form is supposed to work, then of course Garou will take a false positive to raise the child as Garou - they have every reason to think so! Then when the child never changes, it is much more a crushing disappointment.<br /> <br /> Of course, it is always possible to have other Garou shotgun the gift until there is good consensus. However, that is very much a metagame attitude. In actuality, what is more likely is that Scenting a newborn child for parents is a great honor, like being a godfather. It's a honor to do it. You don't take away that person's honor by assuming he'll botch it and having lots of others do it. Besides, botches (or even normal failures) are so rare it's not like Garou expect it to be wrong.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T13:29:42-07:00","id":686113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=683898#post683898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is an easy way to accomplish this. With Scent of True form, the Garou automatically detects a pre-Change Garou as kin. However, if they roll, they have the chance of detecting the pre-Change Garou as really Garou. If the Garou botch the role, they get a false positive or false negative. It's probably best to have the PCs always roll - if they get no successes, then give them the automatic detection - don't give them the automatic success to begin with and then decide whether to roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Scent of the true form&quot; is one of the mechanically least thought out gifts. In earlier versions, the kind of supernatural being determined the difficulty of the gift, meaning, that if you asked for a roll you as ST always gave away that the being wasn't garou and by pronouncing the difficulty you also gave away what kind of supernatural it could or could not be. The only method to avoid that was to have the ST roll for the gift in secret.<br /> <br /> To work fine the gift should have read. Roll against difficulty 6 (in situations where the smell is obscured, like in a full dance club, at a wast processing plant or in heavy wind, the difficulty is increased). Failure means the scent can not be picked up (no retry in that scene). Successes determine what kind of being a person in the scene is, one success is enough for garou, but kin, other fera, mages, sorcerer or vampires all need more successes (bla bla, insert convert from difficulty table). If a garou scores a success but not enough to determine the supernatural being, the gift falls back to what the person appears to be: Animal for fera in animal form, human for almost everything else. Pre-Change garou are at X successes (with X being equal to kin or not, as one prefers).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=683898#post683898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, it is always possible to have other Garou shotgun the gift until there is good consensus. However, that is very much a metagame attitude. In actuality, what is more likely is that Scenting a newborn child for parents is a great honor, like being a godfather. It's a honor to do it. You don't take away that person's honor by assuming he'll botch it and having lots of others do it. Besides, botches (or even normal failures) are so rare it's not like Garou expect it to be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. And I think, that rarely more than one garou with the gift would seek out a distant relative. Besides &quot;Excuse me, may I smell your baby real quick&quot; is kind of an odd question. So there is still a fair chance that plenty kin babies go unnoticed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T21:03:01-07:00","id":689244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=686113#post686113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The only method to avoid that was to have the ST roll for the gift in secret.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true of so many kinds of &quot;divination&quot; abilities. Simply knowing you failed often makes the PCs act differently so a GM has to do it secretly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T08:20:50-07:00","id":691281,"title":"","content":"For most divination gifts I ask for a roll and ask for or see the numbers. I never state a difficulty. I dislike rolling for players my luck runs either extremely hot or cold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T09:00:01-07:00","id":691325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=691281#post691281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For most divination gifts I ask for a roll and ask for or see the numbers. I never state a difficulty. I dislike rolling for players my luck runs either extremely hot or cold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, I hesitate to roll for my players also. Combat is pretty hard to balance given the vagaries of the dice- I have had one of my Garou players nearly get his head stoved in by a spooked horse, due to a lot of exploding 10's on my part and a lot of 1's on his... sometimes that random element has some pretty stupid results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T09:12:56-07:00","id":692543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=691325#post691325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hah, I hesitate to roll for my players also. Combat is pretty hard to balance given the vagaries of the dice- I have had one of my Garou players nearly get his head stoved in by a spooked horse, due to a lot of exploding 10's on my part and a lot of 1's on his... sometimes that random element has some pretty stupid results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truthfully the worst roll I ever made as the ST went something like this: Minor villain a nuisance Hunter who was basically a distraction so the real villain could kidnap a character's sister. Shot at a player. On four dice I rolled four tens, then four more, then three plus a nine. The player then botched the rage roll dead character. <br /> The major villain in my last chronicle a year long story facing down a pack of royally pissed off Garou and what is sure to be an epic fight worthy of songs...I botch all ones on the opening roll...the characters didn't even get a scratch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T15:28:43-07:00","id":696546,"title":"","content":"Ran a VTT 3rd Edition D&amp;D game once on aol... rolled a spot check for someone off scene and he went BALLISTIC insisting on &quot;Rolling his own dice&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T16:54:47-07:00","id":696624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=691281#post691281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For most divination gifts I ask for a roll and ask for or see the numbers. I never state a difficulty. I dislike rolling for players my luck runs either extremely hot or cold.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But Players can open the book and simply know what critters they should have detected with their roll. You not stating the difficulty is somewhat meaningless if it is printed in the book - even if you apply circumstantial adjustments the players have some degree of certainty.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T06:59:29-07:00","id":702040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/659504-not-knowing-which-children-are-garou?p=696624#post696624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. But Players can open the book and simply know what critters they should have detected with their roll. You not stating the difficulty is somewhat meaningless if it is printed in the book - even if you apply circumstantial adjustments the players have some degree of certainty.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true, but then again target numbers vary for several of the gifts: <br /> <br /> Example My players are scouting a popular night club, it is located well within a known vampire feeding area. The players suspect that the bouncers must be working for the leeches or are leeches. They enter the night club and the Philodox uses Sense the Unnatural. I call for a roll. The player rolls, a 6, 5, 7,1, 4, 6, and 8. I state the bouncer appears to be human. Is he a human, a high humanity vampire, a mage, a ghoul or a Hunter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}